---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";

const responsibilities = [
  { title: "Server systems & persistence", detail: "Built server-side features in C# and .NET, modeled persistent data in PostgreSQL, and maintained the validation and safeguards around changes to player state." },
  { title: "Reliability & incident response", detail: "Debugged live issues, investigated performance bottlenecks, and delivered hotfixes while balancing release work with uptime and recovery requirements." },
  { title: "Support & moderation tools", detail: "Built operational interfaces for issue triage, data maintenance, abuse detection, and administrator escalation so the team could investigate and act." },
  { title: "Game design & balance", detail: "Owned game design and balance work alongside engineering, connecting changes to the systems that players experienced in the live world." }
];

const challenges = [
  { title: "Shared state under concurrency", detail: "A live multiplayer environment makes state consistency a practical engineering concern. Long-running sessions, simultaneous actions, and persistent data have to remain coherent as features evolve." },
  { title: "Unpredictable load and behavior", detail: "Peak events and abuse cases create pressure beyond the normal path. Performance tuning, telemetry, validation, and exploit mitigation were part of operating the service." },
  { title: "Changes to a long-lived system", detail: "Feature delivery had to account for backward compatibility, safe data changes, release planning, and rollback. Shipping a change also meant being able to support it in production." }
];
---

<Base title="Eden: Live MMO Engineering - Eric Martin" description="Eric Martin’s work on Eden: C# and .NET server systems, PostgreSQL persistence, game design, support tooling, and reliability in a live multiplayer environment.">
  <section class="page-heading">
    <div class="page-container-mid">
      <a href="/technical-projects" class="text-link">← All projects</a>
      <div class="mt-10 sm:mt-12">
        <p class="eyebrow">Live service / software engineering</p>
        <h1 class="page-title mt-5">Eden</h1>
        <p class="mt-5 max-w-2xl text-2xl font-medium leading-snug text-ink sm:text-3xl">Building and operating a persistent multiplayer world.</p>
        <p class="page-intro mt-6">Eden is a long-running MMO with active players, persistent state, and live uptime expectations. My work combined server engineering, game design, operational tools, and the ongoing responsibility of keeping a shared world running.</p>
        <dl class="surface-muted mt-10 grid gap-8 p-7 sm:mt-12 sm:grid-cols-3 sm:p-9">
          <div><dt class="eyebrow">Community grew to</dt><dd class="mt-4"><span class="block text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight text-accent">~30,000</span><span class="mt-2 block text-sm text-muted">players</span></dd></div>
          <div class="border-t border-border pt-6 sm:border-l sm:border-t-0 sm:pl-7 sm:pt-0"><dt class="eyebrow">Core stack</dt><dd class="mt-4 text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed">C# / .NET<br />PostgreSQL<br />JavaScript</dd></div>
          <div class="border-t border-border pt-6 sm:border-l sm:border-t-0 sm:pl-7 sm:pt-0"><dt class="eyebrow">My role</dt><dd class="mt-4 text-lg font-medium leading-relaxed">Engineering, design, balance, and live operations</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>

      <section class="section-space" aria-labelledby="ownership-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">End-to-end responsibility</p>
        <h2 id="ownership-heading" class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink sm:text-4xl">What I owned</h2>
        <p class="mt-5 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-muted">The work covered the player-facing systems and the tools needed to maintain them. Reliability, support, and product decisions were part of the same engineering responsibility.</p>
        <div class="mt-9 grid gap-x-12 gap-y-8 md:grid-cols-2">
          {responsibilities.map((item) => (
            <article class="border-t border-border pt-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">{item.title}</h3>
              <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{item.detail}</p>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="challenges-heading">
        <p class="eyebrow">Designing for a live world</p>
        <h2 id="challenges-heading" class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink sm:text-4xl">The engineering constraints</h2>
        <div class="mt-8 space-y-4">
          {challenges.map((item) => (
            <article class="surface p-6 sm:p-8">
              <div><h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-ink">{item.title}</h3><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">{item.detail}</p></div>
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section-space grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-2 md:gap-12" aria-labelledby="operations-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Beyond the release</p>
          <h2 id="operations-heading" class="mt-4 text-3xl font-semibold text-ink">Operating the software</h2>
          <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed text-muted">A release was one part of the job. The surrounding work included diagnosing problems, protecting data, maintaining support workflows, and evolving a codebase that had to keep serving players.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="border-t border-border pt-6">
          <ul class="list-disc space-y-4 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted marker:text-accent">
            <li>Structured logging, metrics, and audit trails for investigation</li>
            <li>JavaScript tools for moderation, support, and data maintenance</li>
            <li>GitHub-based build and release automation</li>
            <li>Versioned releases, recovery playbooks, and rollback planning</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="surface-muted p-7 sm:p-10">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold text-ink">How it connects to my other work</h2>
        <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-muted">The same concerns show up in business software: persistent state, clear permissions, useful diagnostics, safe releases, and tools that help a person recover when something goes wrong. Eden is where those concerns met the immediate feedback of a live community.</p>
        <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-3">
          <a href="/abs-tooling" class="text-link">Explore ABS Console <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a href="/contact" class="text-link">Talk about a systems challenge <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
